---
/** `/about/` — copy is AJ's to write (SPEC B2: placeholder until then). */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getAlternates } from '../lib/alternates';
---

<Base title="About" description="About AJ Van Beest." alternates={getAlternates({ kind: 'site' })}>
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="h-display">About</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="body prose">
      <p>I’m AJ Van Beest. I work in cybersecurity, where I build tools to help investigate security alerts. If an AI agent tells me an alert is worth my time, I want it to show me what it found. At home, I’m more likely to ask whether it can play a decent hand of cribbage.</p>
      <p>I used to be a newspaper reporter. These days I sometimes sit on the other side of the interview. When something happens that I want to write about, I’ll have an AI ask me questions. I’m still the one who has to decide whether the story sounds like me.</p>
      <p>A lot of what ends up here starts with something I wanted to do anyway. I wanted to play cards. I needed groceries. My family wanted to watch a show and the media server was down. I’m interested in what happens when I give AI a part in those ordinary bits of my life.</p>
      <p>If you’re curious about my projects or interests, take a look at <a href="https://daemon.ajvanbeest.com/">my daemon</a>. It’s a public profile I built so an AI assistant could get acquainted with me. You can read it, too.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 72px; padding-bottom: 80px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 36px; }
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .page { padding-top: 36px; padding-bottom: 40px; gap: 24px; } }
</style>
